---
import Base from "@layouts/Base.astro";
import Kickoff from "@components/Kickoff.astro";
import TextImageSection from "@components/TextImageSection.astro";
import Section from "@components/Section.astro"

import kickoffPhoto from "@images/kickoff-feb26.jpg"
import tailiasBust from "@images/fursona/Sioteru - Tailias Bust.png"
---

<Base title="From TechGamesPlus to Tailias" description="A post about my change from TGP to Tailias">
    <Kickoff contentAlign="center" backgroundImage={kickoffPhoto} backgroundAlt="A photo of a whiteboard. It contains a teddy bear drawing on the left and text on the right that says '19 Days until FurDU :3'">
        <h1>From TechGamesPlus to Tailias</h1>
        <p>
            From July 28th, 2026, I will be changing from TechGamesPlus to Tailias. This page explains why.
        </p>
    </Kickoff>
    <Section contentAlign="left">
        <p><u>
            Published: <b>July 28th, 2026</b>
        </u></p>
        <p>
            Effective from today (July 28th, 2026), I will be retiring the "TechGamesPlus" branding in favour of my fursona, Tailias. Over the coming days, you'll gradually see the shift between names.
        </p>
    </Section>
    <Section contentAlign="left">
        <h3>
            Retiring the TechGamesPlus Branding
        </h3>
        <p>
            When I was young, I used to always pretend to be an influencer - originally by the name of "MyCraftU2", then to "Da Beef" (for some fucking reason), and then eventually to who I am today: "TechGamesPlus".<br/>
            <br/>
            Yet, for the last few months, I've been falling out of love for the TechGamesPlus name.<br/>
            <br/>
            Nowadays, I'm wanting to diverge away from some 12-year-old's name. I'm older, more mature, and am ready to mature my branding in that way.<br/>
            <br/>
            That's why I'm retiring the "TechGamesPlus" branding.
        </p>
    </Section>
    <TextImageSection imageSide="right" imageSrc={tailiasBust} imageAlt="A photo of a blue bear">
        <h3>
            So why "Tailias"?
        </h3>
        <p>
            For a very long time now, I've been wanting to have a fursona. I actually had four at one point: "Echo", "Delta", "Fenrir", and "Terrah", yet all of them ended up in the graveyard of forgotten fursonas. "Echo" was the only one I actually ended up templating.<br/>
            <br/>
            Terror Teddy was already my prominent avatar. After all, he's a one-of-a-kind creation, made by the local tattoo artist my parents get their tattoo's done by. I love Terror Teddy, and this isn't me saying that I'm getting rid of Terror Teddy.<br/>
            <br/>
            That's why Tailias is a thing. Tailias is meant to be the furry incarnation of Terror Teddy. Originally, that was the responsibility of Terrah (pronounced like "Terror" (see the resemblance??)), but I could never get to that. I always had issues trying to see what design features Terrah could have.<br/>
            <br/>
            I was at a stalemate on making a fursona up until my attendance at <a href="https://furdu.com.au/events/furdu-2026/" target="_blank">FurDU 2026</a>, particularly at <a href="https://www.astrisfursuits.com/" target="_blank">Astris'</a> Guest of Honour panel. She was talking about how to make a fursuit, and it was during that panel that Tailias came to fruition.<br/>
            <br/>
            Tailias is a blue bear, in similar design to Terror Teddy, with the exception of two functioning eyes. He is also part-fox to allow for a longer tail. More details about Tailias can be found on the <a href="fursona">fursona page</a>.
        </p>
    </TextImageSection>
    <Section contentAlign="left">
        <h3>
            What'll happen to the TechGamesPlus brand?
        </h3>
        <p>
            What I aim to achieve in this rebrand from TechGamesPlus to Tailias is to make it a "soft-changeover".<br/>
            <br/>
            That's probably not a proper word, but what I mean is that, simply put: replace all TechGamesPlus with Tailias.<br/>
            <br/>
            Terror Teddy will be effectively retiring from my public life effective from this date. My private socials will still contain him.<br/>
            <br/>
            In terms of Tee Tee, my cartoon mascot, I've made the decision to keep him. I'll be attempting to phase out his assets from long-form videos that I'll potentially make (and yes, I'm gonna get back into making videos again), but that'll be a progressive shift away when I get those assets. He will not be disappearing from the website in his current positions. I've solidified Tee Tee into places I cannot easily remove him from (i.e. letters that I actually write to people), so he'll be remaining. I do have other plans with Tee Tee, however, but I cannot reveal that information just yet.<br/>
            <br/>
            In other words: TechGamesPlus is being discontinued. It won't be removed, I can assure you that. My branding will just switch over to Tailias.
        </p>
    </Section>
    <Section contentAlign="center">
        <h3 style="text-decoration:none">
            Thank You and Goodnight.
        </h3>
    </Section>
</Base>
<style>
    h3 {
        text-decoration: underline;
    }
</style>